# shadcn UI primitives

Interactive chrome (buttons, inputs, dialogs, selects, checkboxes, dropdowns, toasts) comes from shadcn in `components/ui/`. This app uses `components.json` style `base-vega` (Base UI, not Radix).

- Import from `@/components/ui/*`. Do not invent a parallel primitive.
- If the control is missing, add it with `npx shadcn@latest add <name>`, then restyle to berry / milk / blush / yolk like `button.tsx` and `input.tsx`.
- Fix CLI leftovers. Import `cn` from `@/lib/utils`, never from the npm package `cn`. Do not leave default oklch/dark-mode classes on a new primitive.
- Native `<select>`, `<button>`, and raw dialog markup are not substitutes when a shadcn primitive exists or can be added.

```tsx
// BAD
<select value={sort} onChange={...}><option>Likes</option></select>

// GOOD
import { Select, SelectContent, SelectItem, SelectTrigger, SelectValue } from "@/components/ui/select"
```
